 # JSON utility
 
-Run `python cli.py` with JSON on stdin. The identity action returns its value unchanged.
+Run `python cli.py` with one JSON payload on stdin; one JSON result is printed on stdout.
+
+## Actions
+
+- `identity`: `{"action": "identity", "value": <any JSON value>}` returns `value` unchanged.
+- `wrap`: `{"action": "wrap", "text": <string up to 2000 code points>, "width": <int 1..80>}`
+  returns a list of lines. Text is split into paragraphs on literal `\n` (empty
+  paragraphs preserved). Within a paragraph, words are split on whitespace and
+  separators collapsed to one ASCII space; words are greedily placed on lines of
+  at most `width` characters (Python `len`, i.e. Unicode code points). A word
+  longer than `width` occupies its own line intact. Each empty or whitespace-only
+  paragraph contributes one empty string. Input is never mutated; operations are
+  atomic from the caller's perspective.
+
+## Executable CLI example
+
+```
+echo '{"action": "wrap", "text": "the quick brown fox\n\njumps", "width": 9}' | python cli.py
+# -> ["the quick", "brown fox", "", "jumps"]
+```
+
+## Boundary and error semantics
+
+- Boundaries: `width` 1 puts every word on its own line; a word exactly equal to
+  `width` fits on one line; an over-long word stays intact on its own line; empty
+  or whitespace-only paragraphs yield `""` lines.
+- Errors: an unknown action raises `ValueError`; the CLI exits with code 2, prints
+  the error message to nonempty stderr, and prints nothing to stdout (no traceback).
+  Malformed JSON input is handled the same way. No other validation is performed;
+  types/shapes/bounds are otherwise guaranteed.
